{"questions":[{"id":"p1","kind":"path","question":"The scenario starts with `escape("<script>alert(document.cookie);</script>")`. Which branch of `escape` handles this value, what helper does it call, and what exact string does the resulting Markup hold?","key":"Because `type(s) is str` is true (line 39), the fast path is taken: `escape` skips the `__html__` check and the `str(s)` conversion entirely and returns `Markup(_escape_inner(s))`. `_escape_inner` replaces the five characters `& > < ' "`, so the result is `Markup('&lt;script&gt;alert(document.cookie);&lt;/script&gt;')` — the parentheses, semicolons and dots are untouched. The return type is exactly `Markup`.","lines":["src/markupsafe/__init__.py:35-45","src/markupsafe/_native.py:1-8"],"check":"import sys
