"},{"id":"p2","kind":"path","question":"The scenario asserts `escape(safe_comment) == safe_comment` where `safe_comment` is a `Markup`. Which branch does `escape` take, and how many times is `__html__()` invoked during that single `escape()` call?","key":"`type(s) is str` is False (the type is `Markup`, a str subclass), so the `hasattr(s, "__html__")` branch is taken and `Markup(s.__html__())` is returned; `_escape_inner` is never called, so the text is unchanged (escaping is idempotent). `__html__()` runs twice: once in `escape` (line 43) and once again inside `Markup.__new__`, which also checks `hasattr(object, "__html__")` and replaces the object with its result (lines 125-126). This matches trace lines 11-16.","lines":["src/markupsafe/__init__.py:39-45","src/markupsafe/__init__.py:122-134"],"check":"import sys
