"},{"id":"p5","kind":"path","question":"Walk through `Markup("<footer>") + "</p> & <script>oops</script>" + Markup("</footer>")`. What does each `__add__` do to its right-hand operand and what is the final value?","key":"Both additions go through `Markup.__add__`, which accepts the operand because it is a `str` (or has `__html__`) and computes `self.__class__(super().__add__(self.escape(value)))`. The first operand is a plain `str`, so `Markup.escape` escapes it to `&lt;/p&gt; &amp; &lt;script&gt;oops&lt;/script&gt;` (note `&` becomes `&amp;`); the second operand is already a `Markup`, so `escape` returns it unchanged via `__html__`. The final result is `Markup('<footer>&lt;/p&gt; &amp; &lt;script&gt;oops&lt;/script&gt;</footer>')`, of type `Markup`.","lines":["src/markupsafe/__init__.py:136-140","src/markupsafe/__init__.py:230-240"],"check":"import sys
