"},{"id":"p6","kind":"path","question":"`page.striptags()` is called at the end. In what order does `striptags` work, what is the exact returned string for this page, and what is the type of that return value?","key":"`striptags` first loops removing `<!-- ... -->` comments (stopping if no `-->` follows a `<!--`), then loops removing `<`...`>` tags the same way, then collapses all whitespace runs with `" ".join(value.split())`, and finally wraps the text in `self.__class__(...)` only to call `unescape()` on it. The result here is the plain text `User: Alice "The <b>Great</b>" said: <script>alert(document.cookie);</script>` and its type is plain `str` (not `Markup`), because `unescape` returns `html.unescape(str(self))` — so it is unsafe to insert back into HTML without escaping.","lines":["src/markupsafe/__init__.py:199-228","src/markupsafe/__init__.py:188-197"],"check":"import sys
