"},{"id":"p7","kind":"path","question":"Inside `User.__html__`, `Markup('<span class="user">{0}</span>').format(self.name)` is evaluated with `name = 'Alice "The <b>Great</b>"'`. What exactly does the formatted value contain, and why are the quotes in `class="user"` not escaped?","key":"Only the substituted field goes through `EscapeFormatter.format_field`: `name` is a plain `str` with no `__html_format__`/`__html__`, so it falls to `super().format_field(...)` and is then escaped, becoming `Alice &#34;The &lt;b&gt;Great&lt;/b&gt;&#34;` (double quote → `&#34;`). The literal parts of the format string are copied verbatim because the template is already a `Markup`, so the result is `Markup('<span class="user">Alice &#34;The &lt;b&gt;Great&lt;/b&gt;&#34;</span>')`.","lines":["src/markupsafe/__init__.py:313-315","src/markupsafe/__init__.py:339-354"],"check":"import sys
