"},{"id":"p8","kind":"path","question":"The scenario also calls `escape(user)` directly on the `User` object (which defines both `__html__` and `__html_format__`). Which of the two methods does `escape` use, and what is the result?","key":"`escape` never looks at `__html_format__`; after `type(s) is str` fails it checks `hasattr(s, "__html__")` and returns `Markup(s.__html__())`, trusting that output as already safe. So the result is `Markup('<span class="user">Alice &#34;The &lt;b&gt;Great&lt;/b&gt;&#34;</span>')` — the span tag is preserved unescaped while the name was escaped by `User.__html__` itself. `__html_format__` is only consulted by `EscapeFormatter.format_field`.","lines":["src/markupsafe/__init__.py:39-45","src/markupsafe/__init__.py:339-342"],"check":"import sys
